This will update the `name` property of the `jasper` object in your state.

However, if you're using the functional version of setState, which is the recommended way to do it, you can use the following syntax:
```javascript
this.setState(prevState => ({
  jasper: {
   ...prevState.jasper,
    name:'someOtherName'
  }
}));
```
This will update the `name` property of the `jasper` object in your state, and keep the `age` property unchanged.

The reason why your code didn't work is because `setState` is not a replacement for assigning a new value to `this.state`. It's a method that merges the new state with the current state.

